<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 24px;">[24]7.ai Asset Tracker - Documentation Index</h1>

The master Technical Architecture and System Engineering documentation for the <strong>[24]7.ai Asset Tracking &amp; Clearance Gateway System</strong> is maintained in:

<li><strong>Primary Architecture Document:</strong> <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">/opt/asset-tracker-docs/TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md</code></li>
<li><strong>Workspace Architecture Copy:</strong> <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">./TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md</code></li>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 16px;">Document Contents:</h3>
1. Executive Summary &amp; Problem Space
2. Global System Architecture Diagram
3. Frontend Technology Stack &amp; Client Architecture (React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, html5-qrcode, USB HID)
4. Node.js Backend Integration &amp; API Services (Express.js, REST Controllers, Gate Verification)
5. Reverse Proxy Architecture: Nginx with SSL/TLS (Port 80 to 443 Redirect, Security Headers, Upstream Proxy)
6. End-to-End Data Flow &amp; Audit Compliance Matrix (ISO 27001 &amp; SOC 2 Type II Alignment)
7. Storage Engine &amp; Mutex-Locked Atomic Persistence
8. Host Service Management &amp; Systemd Daemon
9. Performance Benchmarks &amp; Capacity Limits (&lt; 1.5ms Gate Scan Latency)
10. Disaster Recovery Runbook (RTO &lt; 2 minutes)

